  "notes": "VERIFIED. Two independent authoritative sources agree hole-for-hole, tee-for-tee, and on both men's and ladies' stroke indexes: (1) the operator's own published Complete Course Guide PDF on savannahgolflinks.ca, and (2) the Golf Canada / Golf Ontario course-rating database record for the facility (embedded JSON on the Golf Canada facility page, tee IDs 213581/583/585/587 men's and 213582/584/586/588 women's). Internal checks pass: per-hole yardages sum exactly to the four published totals (6213 / 5833 / 5463 / 4563), which also match the club's own course-details summary table and GolfPass; par sums to 71 (36 out / 35 in); men's and ladies' stroke indexes are each a complete 1-18 with odd on the front nine and even on the back. Single 18-hole course (Golf Canada classifies it 'EighteenHole') - no second course or extra nine to conflate. DISAGREEMENT: BlueGolf's detailed scorecard publishes a materially different and apparently stale card (Gold 6090 / Blue 5705 / White 5313 / Red 4395, with different per-hole yardages such as hole 3 Gold 136 vs 143 and hole 2 Gold 615 vs 613) and carries no stroke-index data at all (all -1); its women's par of 73 with holes 7 and 8 as par 5 is contradicted by both primary sources. BlueGolf's figures were NOT used. MINOR DISCREPANCY: the club's course guide labels hole 18 'Par 5/R4', implying par 4 from the Red tees (Red par 70), but Golf Canada's women's Red rating record carries hole 18 as par 5 and a total par of 71. Par 71 is used here for all tees. CAVEAT: the operator's course guide PDF was authored in 2013; the Golf Canada rating record independently corroborates every number, but the tee records are flagged isActive:false in that dataset, so the ratings may be from a rating cycle that has since lapsed rather than a current re-rating."
